Actually, there's a further complication: I just realized that every possible
mechanism for identifying runners up will be completely pathological at the
beginning of the tournament.  This would straighten itself out within the first
24 hours (and probably within the first hour), but until there's enough
seperation in the games _everybody_ could be a runner-up.  This would result
in, for example, a scenario where most unique deaths would be 2 and everyone
who's died once would be listed as a runner up making for a _huge_ scoreboard
page.

I need to think a bit more about how to deal with this.

I'm thinking we should probably have two scoreboards, one of which would show
runners up and the other would show only winners?

